OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F431A1787617145
OL,3,CCyclist Josh Tarling to ride in place
OL,4,Cof brother, 19, who died during race
OL,6,FThe older brother of a 19-year-old who
OL,7,Fdied in a serious accident during a
OL,8,Fcycling race in Portugal, will ride
OL,9,Fthe race in his sibling's honour.
OL,11,FWelsh track and road cyclist Josh
OL,12,FTarling, 22, is set to ride in the
OL,13,FVuelta a Espana after his brother
OL,14,FFinlay died when a collision occurred
OL,15,Fwith a non-race, light goods vehicle -
OL,16,Fwhich had entered the course on August
OL,17,F14.
